{"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/segmentspecencoding"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Segment, RudderStack and Customer.io Data Pipelines each take the same batch call of the Segment"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"spec, at endpoints of their own. One encoder, "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/SegmentSpecBatchEncoder"},{"type":"text","text":", writes it, and a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"factory for each fills in the endpoint and how the key travels:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/segment(writeKey:region:plan:backoff:clock:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" posts to the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"\/v1\/batch","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" of the workspace’s region (","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/SegmentRegion","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":"), with the write key as HTTP Basic","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"authentication’s user name and an empty password.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/rudderStack(writeKey:dataPlane:plan:backoff:clock:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" posts to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the "},{"code":"\/v1\/batch","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" of your data plane URL, with the write key the same way."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/customerIO(apiKey:region:plan:backoff:clock:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" posts to the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Pipelines API’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"\/v1\/batch","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in the workspace’s region (","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/CustomerIORegion","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":"), with the key as a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"bearer token and ","type":"text"},{"code":"X-Strict-Mode: 1","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each splits a batch to the spec’s limits ("},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/SegmentSpecBatchEncoder\/batchLimit"},{"type":"text","text":"): 2,500 calls"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and 500 KB a request, and under 32 KB a call, which all three accept. A batch with no record the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"encoder can write, an empty one included, makes no request. Each retries no response, a 5xx, 408"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and 429, and drops and reports any other status. No trace context is sent. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"import Traffluent"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"leaves this module out; import it on its own."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The key goes in the "},{"code":"Authorization","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" header field, never in the body. It is a public client key:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Segment’s and RudderStack’s write keys, and Customer.io’s public keys ("},{"code":"pk_…","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"), ship in their"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vendors’ own app and web libraries, and they let a client send data to the source and read"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"nothing."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Customer.io’s private keys ("},{"code":"sk_…","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":") reach every Customer.io API, deleting people included, so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the factory throws "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/CustomerIOSetupError\/privateKey"},{"type":"text","text":" for one. Each factory throws for an empty"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"key ("},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/SegmentSetupError"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/RudderStackSetupError"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/CustomerIOSetupError"},{"type":"text","text":"), RudderStack’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"for a data plane URL that isn’t a plain "},{"code":"https","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" URL, and Customer.io’s for a public key of the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"other region."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A region has no default. Segment and Customer.io keep a workspace’s data in the US or the EU, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"events posted to the other region’s endpoint don’t reach it, so you pick the region on purpose.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Each record becomes a track call of an anonymous user. Its ","type":"text"},{"code":"anonymousId","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is the record’s session,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"from the sessions enricher; a record with no session is sent under its own record identifier. No","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"userId","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"identify","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" call or traits are sent. Its ","type":"text"},{"code":"messageId","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is the record’s identifier, which","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a redelivered record keeps, and its ","type":"text"},{"code":"timestamp","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" the record’s timestamp in ISO 8601 with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"milliseconds. The record’s vendor identifier and trace context aren’t sent. The standard context","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"goes in the spec’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"context","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" fields (","type":"text"},{"code":"app","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"device","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"locale","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"network","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"os","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"), with no","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"device.id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":"advertisingId","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every call’s "},{"code":"context.ip","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"code":"0.0.0.0","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", which Segment takes in place of the request’s address, so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it records none. RudderStack fills in a "},{"code":"request_ip","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" from the request unless the call has one,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"even beside "},{"code":"context.ip","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and passes it on to its destinations, so RudderStack’s calls also carry"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"request_ip","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" as "},{"code":"0.0.0.0","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". Customer.io’s references don’t say whether "},{"code":"context.ip","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" takes the place"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of the address it reads from an HTTP request, so it may still record the request’s."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Each endpoint counts a user per ","type":"text"},{"code":"anonymousId","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so each session is one user in its reports, and so","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is each record sent without a session. On a plan billed by monthly tracked users, each counts as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"one. A record a store recovers after a relaunch keeps its session, so it goes out under the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"anonymousId","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"messageId","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" of its first send. Segment deduplicates calls by ","type":"text"},{"code":"messageId","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"drops most duplicates within about 24 hours, not all, so one it stored before the app ended is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"most likely not stored again. RudderStack’s and Customer.io’s API references don’t say whether","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"they deduplicate, so such a record may be stored twice there.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Properties are read through the event’s schema in the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TrackingPlan"},{"text":" the encoder is made with. A","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sensitive"},{"text":" value is never sent, whatever the record reveals. A record the encoder can’t write is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"left out and the rest of the batch is sent: one the plan doesn’t describe, one named as one of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Customer.io’s semantic events, which delete or suppress people and devices (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"User Deleted"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"User Suppressed"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Device Deleted"},{"text":" and the rest), one whose event isn’t ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Encodable"},{"text":", one holding","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a value JSON can’t, one whose timestamp has no ISO 8601 form, and one too large for a call. The","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"destination reports each as ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDropReport.skipped(_:)"},{"text":", a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SkippedRecord"},{"text":" whose reason is a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/SegmentSpecEncodingError","type":"reference"},{"text":", and the encoder logs a notice for each semantic event name in the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"plan when the destination is made.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Segment answers 200 for every request but one too large or not JSON, so a wrong region, a write","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"key of no source, or a batch of more calls than it takes may be answered 200 with nothing stored.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Check the source’s debugger after setting the destination up. RudderStack answers a wrong write","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"key with 401, and Customer.io, in strict mode, with 401 too, so the destination reports those. In","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"strict mode Customer.io refuses a whole batch for one bad call, so the encoder leaves out each call","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Customer.io documents refusing; a 400 for anything else drops the whole request.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"To send to PostHog, Amplitude or Mixpanel, use "},{"code":"PostHogEncoding","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"AmplitudeEncoding","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"MixpanelEncoding","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" instead."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["import HTTPDestinations","import SegmentSpecEncoding","import TrackingPlans","","let plan = try TrackingPlan()","let segment = try HTTPDestination.segment(","    writeKey: writeKey,","    region: .us,  \/\/ or .eu, where the workspace is","    plan: plan)","let tracker = Tracker(enrichers: [.sessions()])","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(to: segment)"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The guide "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/choosingdestinations","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"covers what each endpoint receives, and why, in more detail."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"sections":[],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/segment(writeKey:region:plan:backoff:clock:)","doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentatio